<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<app version="1">
  <name>Fuse</name>
  <coder>Philip Kendall, Bjoern Giesler, Juan Francisco Roco and the Fuse team</coder>
  <version>@VERSION@</version>
  <release_date>@RELEASE_DATE@</release_date>
  <short_description>ZX Spectrum emulator</short_description>
  <long_description>Fuse, the Free Unix Spectrum Emulator, emulates the Sinclair ZX Spectrum 16K, 48K, 128K, +2, +2A, +3 and many clones, together with a wide range of peripherals.

Homepage: https://fuse-emulator.sourceforge.net

Controls (Wii Remote held sideways, 1 and 2 buttons on the right):
- HOME: open the menu
- D-pad: move through menus and files; joystick in games
- 1: select a menu entry or file
- 2: go back / cancel

Load games (.z80, .sna, .tzx, .tap and more) from the SD card with File -&gt; Open. To play with the Wii Remote, choose a joystick type in Options -&gt; Joysticks and select the same one in the game.

Options -&gt; Save stores the settings in sd:/apps/fuse/fuserc; to save them automatically on exit, tick Options -&gt; General -&gt; Auto-save settings.

To quit, open the menu and choose File -&gt; Exit.

Known limitations:
- USB keyboard support has not been tested on real hardware yet
- The PAL TV and NTSC TV display filters are not available</long_description>
</app>
